## Native selection and composition

Follow-ups from PR #1573, in this order:

1. Full-table selection, a selected diagram before empty prose, and an inline
   image at the end of its paragraph or alone in it can restart Chromium
   composition: provisional `ni` survives beside committed `你`. Moving the caret
   inside `compositionstart` causes the restart. The follow-up should replace
   that relocation with a valid native caret projection before composition, not
   filter provisional text or add per-object cases.
2. A diagram-only or figure-only document can lose its native DOM range after
   mouseup while ProseMirror keeps a NodeSelection. Chromium then emits no input
   events. Fix the missing browser input target without per-object event patches.

Reproduce with real selection plus Chromium `Input.imeSetComposition` updates and
commit. This does not verify Android InputConnection or an operating-system IME.
